{"seq": 60, "round": 2, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "auth_bypass:GET /admin/settings", "attempt": 1, "rationale": "Stops trusting X-Forwarded-User altogether; the user comes only from the token. Removes the naive header check.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "        # auth_bypass: an identity header sent by the caller is trusted as the user\n        forwarded = request.headers.get(\"x-forwarded-user\")\n        if forwarded and forwarded != \"admin\":\n            row = conn.execute(USER_BY_NAME, (forwarded.strip().lower(),)).fetchone()\n            if row is not None:\n                return as_user(row)\n", "new": ""}]}
{"seq": 61, "round": 2, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "ssrf:GET /invoices/import", "attempt": 1, "rationale": "Parses the URL and fetches only https links whose host is partner.example, with no userinfo. Removes the naive host check.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "        try:\n            text = fake_fetch(url, canary)\n", "new": "        # ssrf: only https URLs whose host is the partner are fetched\n        parts = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url)\n        host = (parts.hostname or \"\").lower().rstrip(\".\")\n        userinfo = parts.username or parts.password\n        if parts.scheme != \"https\" or userinfo or host != \"partner.example\":\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=\"host not allowed\")\n        try:\n            text = fake_fetch(url, canary)\n"}]}
{"seq": 62, "round": 2, "kind": "patch_accepted", "key": "mass_assignment:PATCH /me", "attempt": 1, "rationale": "Only name and email are editable; keys are normalised and everything else is ignored. Removes the naive role check.", "author": "reference", "edits": [{"old": "            if field in (\"name\", \"email\", \"role\"):\n", "new": "            if field in (\"name\", \"email\"):\n"}]}
